## 4. Pitfalls & Invariants
- **Fail-Closed Licensing**: If license detection cannot confirm a permissive license with 100% confidence, the engine defaults to Track 2 Clean-Room Isolation.
- **No Absolute Paths**: All generated skills, digests, and sanitized code must strictly pass the relative path invariant check.
- **SCONES URL Hygiene vs Absolute Paths**: Security checkers that block `/Users/...` or local paths must not falsely flag GitHub HTTPS URLs (`https://github.com/...`). Ensure regexes distinguish protocol URIs from local filesystem paths.
- **Pydantic Class Identifier Sanitization**: Class names generated from repo slugs containing hyphens (e.g. `agent-skills`) must be sanitized into valid CamelCase identifiers (`AgentSkillsConfig`), avoiding invalid syntax like `Agent-SkillsConfig(BaseModel)`.
- **Hermes Runtime Skill Registration**: Assimilated skills saved to `core/skills/<repo>_assimilated/` must be registered or mirrored into `core/orchestrator/agents/gerych_prime/skills/<category>/<name>_assimilated/` so the active Hermes CLI agent and swarm workers can discover and view them via `skill_view`.
- **Deep Reference Harvester Fallback**: Never query `/contents/skills` exclusively. Repositories without a `skills/` directory must cascade through `docs/`, `spec/`, `architecture/`, and root technical documentation (`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `API.md`) to avoid the 0-file "Hollow Skill" trap.
- **Concrete Runtime Rule Activation**: Assimilation must bridge into active worker configs via `activate_assimilation_slice()`, generating `assimilated_conversion_rules.json` and `assimilated_audit_rules.json` that are dynamically consumed by `services/dnk_shopify` and `core/security/adversarial_review.py`.
- **Swarm Mapping Integrity**: Repositories must not default to generic media workers unless visual/video frameworks (Remotion, WebGL, Canvas) are explicitly detected.
